From 19b88d51840380a9680164aa2a7f440b97ecd124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:34:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] oneshot: `hermes -z` started during a core-update
 swap waits for the restarted gateway
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A finite run (`hermes -z`, `chat -q`) started while an instant core update swapped the gateway exited at
once with `Error: Gateway draining: update_paused` and lost its prompt (hermes-hub 2026-11-12 17:54Z and
18:02Z, found in the live proof of t_01a1d08863024254). A one-shot that was already running waits up to
10 min for the restarted owner (`GatewayChatView._redial`); a new one did not, so selfheal probes and
scripts running `hermes -z` on a timer failed on every apply.

New `hermes_cli/gateway_update_wait.UpdateWait`: a finite run retries the refusals that admit nothing
while an update swaps the owner, for at most 10 min from the first one, with one stderr notice
(none in stream-json):
- ensure's `draining` (update_paused, restart_wait, replaced) / `starting` verdicts on the dial, and,
  once waiting, a refused or half-started dial;
- a draining owner's `runtime_draining` / `runtime_retired` answer to runtime.describe /
  session.create / session.resume (that attempt's connection is closed, the next owner is asked again);
- the same answer to `prompt.submit` (`GatewayChatView._submit_finite`): dial the next owner,
  re-attach the same session and submit again.
Any other refusal, a dial failure before any update refusal, and interactive chats keep the old exit.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_gateway_chat_update_wait.py — 10 tests; on the previous source 5 fail
(the update_paused wait, the window bound, both session refusals, the refused submit), with the
change all pass. Every test file importing gateway_chat / gateway_chat_view / gateway_update_wait
(41 files, 451 tests) passes; scripts/check --only health ok.
